Package: mica-apid
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: mos build <mos@example.invalid>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: micad (= @VERSION@), mica-system
Description: mos API daemon
 Serves the web dashboard over HTTPS and makes every state change through
 micad's D-Bus interface rather than by touching the system itself.
 .
 /usr/bin/mica-apid is a link to /usr/bin/micad: one binary serves both daemons and
 selects apid by the name it is invoked as, so this package ships no ELF and
 asks for no shlibs substitution.
 .
 The dependencies are pinned to the exact version because apid and micad are
 built from one workspace commit and speak an interface that carries no
 compatibility promise across commits, while mica-system owns the writable
 /mica mount that apid requires for custom UI packages.
 .
 The package owns its enablement: apid.service and the
 multi-user.target.wants symlink that starts it are both payload, so
 installing this package is what makes the daemon run.
